# Mobility Maps from Google Location History

**Road usage, place visits, and spatial intensity maps**

This project turns **Google Maps Location History** into high-quality spatial maps showing:

* Roads you **frequent** vs roads you **never used**
* Places you spend time at (time-weighted)
* Visit purpose (POIs: cafés, universities, hospitals, etc.)
* Continuous spatial intensity fields (KDE / hexbin)
* Weekday vs weekend mobility patterns

All outputs are publication-ready (600 DPI PNGs).

---

## 1. Input data: Google Maps Location History

### How to export your data

1. Go to **Google Takeout**
   [https://takeout.google.com](https://takeout.google.com)
2. Select **Location History**
3. Choose **JSON format**
4. Download and extract the archive
5. Locate the file named something like:

   ```
   Location History/Records.json
   ```
6. Rename or copy it into the project folder as:

   ```
   location-history.json
   ```

That file is the **only required input**.

---

## 2. Environment setup

### Python version

* Python **3.9+** recommended

### Required libraries

Install once:

```bash
pip install numpy pandas matplotlib geopandas shapely osmnx scikit-learn rasterio contextily arabic-reshaper python-bidi
```

> ⚠️ OSMnx relies on the public **Overpass API**.
> Large regions or `network_type="all"` may take time.

